  "content": "<p><strong>Unit 4 - Rates â€” Title &amp; Goal</strong><br />Comprehensive lesson covering Unit 4 - Rates for SAT Math preparation.</p>\n\n\n<h3>Key idea</h3>\n<p>Read the idea and scan the rules. Focus on how the symbols behave.</p>\n<p>A <strong>rate</strong> compares two different quantities with different units.</p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mtext>Rate</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>QuantityÂ A</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>QuantityÂ B</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>\n<ul>\n<li>Always include units - many traps involve mismatched units.  </li>\n<li>For combined rates, <strong>add rates, not times</strong>.  </li>\n<li>For ratios in word problems, set up proportions.  </li>\n<li>Convert early to avoid mistakes (miles â†’ feet, hours â†’ minutes).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>1) A runner covers 10 km in 50 minutes. What is her speed in km/h?<br/>\n2) Convert 5 feet to inches.<br/>\n3) A car travels 150 miles in 2.5 hours. Find speed in mph.<br/>\n4) A faucet fills a tub in 15 minutes, another in 20 minutes. How long together?<br/>\n5) A cyclist rides 12 miles in 40 minutes. Find unit rate in miles per hour.</p>\n<p>1) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>50</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow></math> km/min â†’ <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mi>Ã—</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math> km/h<br/>\n2) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>ft</mtext><mi>Â·</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>in</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>ft</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>in</mtext></mrow></math><br/>\n3) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>150</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2.5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow></math> mph<br/>\n4) Rates: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math> tubs/min. Time = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>â‰ˆ</mo><mn>8.57</mn></mrow></math> min<br/>\n5) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>40</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow></math> miles/min â†’ <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mi>Ã—</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></math> mph</p>\n\n<h3>Worked example</h3>\n<p>Follow the steps carefully, then try to reproduce them without looking.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples</strong>\n- Speed = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mtext>distance</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>time</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math><br/>\n- Density = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mtext>mass</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>volume</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math><br/>\n- Price per item = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mtext>cost</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>numberÂ ofÂ items</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math> </p>\n<p>A <strong>unit rate</strong> expresses the rate per 1 unit.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples</strong>\n- 180 miles in 3 hours â†’ <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>180</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow></math> miles/hour<br/>\n- \\<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>12</mn><mi>f</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>4</mn><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>â†’</mi></mrow></math>\\dfrac{12}{4} = 3$ dollars/pound  </p>\n<p>A <strong>conversion factor</strong> is a fraction equal to 1, used to change units.  </p>\n<p><strong>Common examples</strong>\n- <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>hour</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>minutes</mtext></mrow></math><br/>\n- <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>inch</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>2.54</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow></math><br/>\n- <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>mile</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>5280</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>ft</mtext></mrow></math> </p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong><br/>\nConvert 5 hours to minutes:</p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>hr</mtext><mi>Â·</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>min</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>hr</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>min</mtext></mrow></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mtext>Distance</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>Rate</mtext><mi>Ã—</mi><mtext>Time</mtext></mrow></math>\n<ul>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></math> </li>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math> </li>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math> </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong><br/>\nIf speed is 50 mph for 3 hours:</p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mi>Ã—</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>miles</mtext></mrow></math>\n<p><strong>Example 1: Travel</strong><br/>\nA car travels 180 miles in 3 hours. What is its speed?  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>180</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>mph</mtext></mrow></math>\n<p><strong>Example 2: Conversion</strong><br/>\nHow many seconds in 2 hours?  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>hr</mtext><mi>Â·</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>min</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>hr</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mi>Â·</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>s</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>min</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>7200</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>s</mtext></mrow></math>\n<p><strong>Example 3: Combined Rates</strong><br/>\nIf Pipe A fills a tank in 4 hours, Pipe B fills the same tank in 6 hours, how long if both work together?<br/>\nRates: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mtext>Â </mtext><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math>. Combined = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math>.<br/>\nTime = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>2.4</mn></mrow></math> hours.</p>\n\n<h3>Quick practice</h3>\n<p>Try these on your own. Check your steps, not just the final answer.</p>\n1) A runner covers 10 km in 50 minutes. What is her speed in km/h?<br/>\n<br />\n1) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>50</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow></math> km/min â†’ <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>0.2</mn><mi>Ã—</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math> km/h<br/>\n\n2) Convert 5 feet to inches.<br/>\n<br />\n2) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>ft</mtext><mi>Â·</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>in</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>ft</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mtext>Â </mtext><mtext>in</mtext></mrow></math><br/>\n\n3) A car travels 150 miles in 2.5 hours. Find speed in mph.<br/>\n<br />\n3) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>150</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2.5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow></math> mph<br/>\n\n<h3>Mixed practice set</h3>\n<p>These mix everything above. Time yourself and reflect on any mistakes.</p>\n\n4) A faucet fills a tub in 15 minutes, another in 20 minutes. How long together?<br/>\n<br />\n4) Rates: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math> tubs/min. Time = <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>â‰ˆ</mo><mn>8.57</mn></mrow></math> min<br/>\n\n5) A cyclist rides 12 miles in 40 minutes. Find unit rate in miles per hour.\n<br />\n5) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>40</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow></math> miles/min â†’ <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mi>Ã—</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></math> mph",
